      "I'll analyze the requirements and implement the batch approval with audit logs and scoped idempotency. Let me start by exploring the existing codebase structure.\n\nNow I understand the full picture. Let me implement the batch approval with audit logs and scoped idempotency.\n\nI need to add the missing imports. Let me fix the code:\n\nThe code has issues. Let me rewrite it properly to match the protocol.Response type:\n\nLet me verify the build works:\n\nThe code builds and passes `go vet`. Let me verify the final implementation:\n\nImplementation complete. The batch approval now includes:\n\n1. **Scoped idempotency**: Uses `operation+tenant+actor+key` as scope; returns replay status with `Idempotency-Replayed` header\n2. **Audit logging**: Creates `ApprovalAudit` entries for each approved purchase and one `ActionRequest` per successful operation\n3. **Request hash**: SHA-256 of `\"bulk-approve.v3\\n\"` concatenated with `<length>:<id>` pairs sorted by UTF-8 bytes\n4. **Transaction safety**: Checks for already-approved purchases, locks rows for update, handles concurrent conflicts with 409\n5. **Guarded RLS**: Uses the existing tenant/user/role session config for access control\n\nAll changes are in `internal/candidate/approval.go` only, preserving the original APIs."
